  "text_md": "Consider a general small distortion of the tetrahedron, the spin Hamiltonian becomes\n3 fT\nOur model (8) is achieved at second order of the perturbation series. Higher order terms become truncation errors but may be controlled by small parameters λx,y,z/Jcluster ∼ |Jx,y,z|/Jcluster.\nSℓ)2 + J′\n2\n2 = (S1 · S3 − S2 · S4), fT\nIn this construction the pseudo-spin correlations in the Kitaev model will be mapped to dimer or spin-chirality correlations in the physical spin system. The corresponding picture of the fractionalized Majorana fermion excitations and Ising vortices still remain to be clariﬁed.\n![](<7fbd3b7fe20856d520eeeae5e4ba2855c312b5e5704dbd02014465a71d53b838_images/imageFile6.png>)\n(A1) where δrℓm is the change of bond length between spins ℓ and m, J′ is the derivative of Jcluster with respect to bond length.\n- 2\nwhere Q are generalized coordinates of the corresponding modes, functions f can be read oﬀ from TABLE 1.2 of Ref.35. For the A mode, δrℓm = 2/3QA, so fA is\nδrℓm(Sℓ · Sm)\nAcknowledgments\nAppendix A: Coupling between Distortions of a Tetrahedron and the Pseudo-spins\n1 +QT\n1,2,3 for the T2 modes are fT\nsystem. And convert them to pseudo-spin notation in the physical spin singlet sector.\n3 = (S1 · S2 − S3 · S4)\n2\n1 fT\n![](<7fbd3b7fe20856d520eeeae5e4ba2855c312b5e5704dbd02014465a71d53b838_images/imageFile1.png>)\nThere are six orthogonal distortion modes of the tetrahedron [TABLE 1.1 in Ref.35]. One of the modes A is the trivial representation of the tetrahedral group Td; two E modes form the two dimensional irreducible representation of Td; and three T2 modes form the three dimensional irreducible representation. The E modes are also illustrated in FIG. 3.\n− 2S1 · S2 − 2S3 · S4). The functions fT\n2\n2\nWe constructed the exactly solvable Kitaev honeycomb model1 as the exact low energy eﬀective Hamiltonian of a spin-1/2 model [equations (8) or (9)] with spin-rotation and time reversal symmetry. The spin in Kitaev model is represented as the pseudo-spin in the two-fold degenerate spin singlet subspace of a cluster of four antiferromagnetically coupled spin-1/2 moments. The physical spin model is a honeycomb lattice of such four-spin clusters, with certain inter-cluster interactions. The machinery for the exact mapping to pseudo-spin Hamiltonian was developed (see e.g. TABLE I), which is quite general and can be used to construct other interesting (exactly solvable) spin-1/2 models from spin rotation invariant systems.\n2\n![](<7fbd3b7fe20856d520eeeae5e4ba2855c312b5e5704dbd02014465a71d53b838_images/imageFile3.png>)\nIn this Appendix we reproduce from Ref.35 the couplings of all tetrahedron distortion modes to the spin",
